PRO-FORMA FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS RESOLUTION

WHEREAS, the Company, a wholly foreign-owned enterprise to be formed as a limited liability company under the laws of Taiwan, has received the approval of the Investment Commission of the Ministry of Economic Affairs and is now taking the final steps for statutory incorporation;

WHEREAS, the sole subscribing shareholder has proposed to subscribe for, and pay in full, all of the issued shares of the Company, and the board has reviewed the bank deposit certificate and the capital contribution schedule;

WHEREAS, the Company has selected a registered office and statutory seat in Taipei City, Taiwan, and the lease term and address have been approved by the shareholder;

WHEREAS, the Company requires a primary corporate banking relationship and treasury instructions, and the directors must appoint officers capable of signing and executing banking documents and statutory filings;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, ADOPTED AND CONFIRMED as follows:

1. Share Capital Subscription and Issuance: The board ratifies and adopts the subscription of the Company's authorized and issued share capital of [insert amount], divided into [insert number] fully paid ordinary shares. All such shares have been subscribed for cash by the sole shareholder, and the corresponding funds have been received, deposited, and certified by [name of certified public accountant]. The board authorizes the issuance of share certificates and the maintenance of the capital verification record in the statutory corporate minute book.

2. Registered Office Adoption: The board designates [insert address], Taipei City, Taiwan, as the Company's registered office and principal place of business. The chairperson and corporate secretary are jointly authorized to execute the lease, to receive legal process and official correspondence, and to file any address change with the Department of Commercial Affairs at the Ministry of Economic Affairs as required by law.

3. Banking Authorization: The board designates [bank name and branch] as the principal depository bank. The chairperson, together with any one other appointed director or senior officer listed in this resolution, are authorized to open current accounts, sign cheques, execute wire transfers, sign foreign exchange forms, and administer online banking tokens, within the limit of [amount] per transaction; any excess must be approved by the board before execution.

4. Statutory Officers: The following officers are appointed: [Name] as Chairperson and Managing Director; [Name] as Director and General Manager; [Name] as Corporate Secretary and Compliance Officer; and [Name] as Chief Financial Officer. The officers are authorized to represent the Company before the Investment Commission, the Ministry of Economic Affairs, the National Taxation Bureau, the Central Bank, banks, and all administrative agencies, and to execute all filings required under the Taiwan Company Act and the Foreign Investment Act.

5. Authorization to File: The corporate secretary and the external certified public accountant are directed to file the incorporation registration, tax registration, labor insurance registration, health insurance registration, bank account activation, and any foreign exchange declarations, and to do all acts necessary to complete the formation and maintain legal existence.

This resolution is effective as of [date], shall be recorded in the minutes of the first meeting, and may be relied upon by banks, agencies, and counterparties.
